  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/neolissochilus-stracheyi-blue-tor-2/",
      "html": "<p>A splendid large barb from Burma (Myanmar), reaching a maximum size of approx. 60 cm. The extremely large, diamond-shaped blue scales on the back shine brightly in a swimming fish, and the orange-red stripe on the side looks gorgeous. Under flash photography from the front the fish looks rather drab silvery; the colours can be shown in photos only in slightly underexposed pictures and grazing light.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/neolissochilus-stracheyi-blue-tor-2/",
      "html": "<p>Neolissochilus inhabit rivers in primary forests of subtropical regions of northern India, Burma, Thailand and most probably Cambodia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/neolissochilus-stracheyi-blue-tor-2/",
      "html": "<p>The water in their habitats is always very clean, and the fish are known to disappear when human activities (clearing, water pollution) increase.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/neolissochilus-stracheyi-blue-tor-2/",
      "html": "<p>Due to its geographical distribution the species is adapted to water temperatures between 16 and 26°C. It is already a much sought-after fish for koi carp ponds in tropical Asia (at temperatures between 22 and 24°C).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/neolissochilus-stracheyi-blue-tor-2/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Neolissochilus: ancient Greek, means \"new Lissochilus\"; Lissochilus is another genus of barb. stracheyi: dedication name. Blue Tor: the common name refers to the large blue scales on the back and the overall similarity of the fish to the members of the carp genus Tor.</p>"
    }
  ],
